setting-component: government

Nominal Control: Elgari Agroeconomic Council

Functional Governance:

Rural Zones: Loosely managed by agricultural co-ops (some backed by Starbucks, others independent)

Urban Hubs: Controlled by regional Elgari prefects, often deeply corrupt or overwhelmed

Starbucks Influence: Massive—functions as co-government in coffee regions, controls much of the transportation infrastructure and land rights through debt and contract clauses

Resistance Elements: A small but organized Agrosyndicalist Network has been gaining traction in rural zones. They protest Starbucks land ownership expansion and biotech licensing fees.
